# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Today's Dockerfile copies named globs — `COPY *.py .` and `COPY src/*.py src/` — so none of the
# paths below could reach the runtime image anyway. This file is still worth having for two
# separate reasons:
#
#   * everything not listed here is packed up and shipped to the docker daemon as build context on
#     every single build, including `.git` and whatever a developer happens to have under data/;
#   * the day somebody replaces those globs with a `COPY . .` — the single most common Dockerfile
#     edit there is — this file is the only thing standing between the repo's working tree and a
#     published image. Two of the entries below would be actively harmful in that image, and both
#     are called out where they appear.

.git
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.py[cod]

# NOT merely noise. `get_settings()` calls `load_dotenv()`, which reads a `.env` from the working
# directory — so a `.env` baked into the image would silently supply BOT_TOKEN and the LLM keys to
# every container started from it. That is a developer's own credentials shipped inside a published
# image, and it also disables the startup guard: the container would come up "fine" while pointed
# at the wrong bot. The smoke gate would catch it (its three no-environment runs would stop exiting
# non-zero), but it must not get that far.
.env

# Other people's CalDAV passwords. src/users.py stores each user's calendar credentials as
# PLAINTEXT JSON in data/user_<id>.json; in production that directory is a mounted volume, and on a
# developer's machine it is whatever was left there by a local run. This repository is public and
# its images are published, so this line is the one that keeps a local test account's calendar
# password out of a public image layer.
data/

# Tests never run in the image, and one of them (tests/test_llm.py) drives a live, paid LLM API —
# see the note at the top of both workflows in .gitea/workflows/.
tests/
requirements-dev.txt

# CI belongs to the repository, not to the artifact. `.github/` stays listed although its workflow
# has been removed: a mirror or a lint workflow reappearing there should not become a build input.
.github/
.gitea/
ci/

*.md
LICENSE
docker-compose.yml
.DS_Store
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
pyrightconfig.json
